From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: somestupidgirl <sunnevanattsol@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 16:12:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] libutil: port login_cap/getcap family from FreeBSD for
 Darwin

Import the login.conf capability-database machinery from FreeBSD
(lib/libutil, freebsd-src main) so that the Darwin command line tools
which depend on it -- su(1), login(1), newgrp(1), atrun(8),
calendar(1) -- can build against our own libutil instead of relying on
Apple's private implementation.

New files:
- getcap.c          cgetent(3) family: text-mode login.conf parser,
                    tc= recursion, boolean/#num/=str/=list lookups.
- login_cap.c       login_getclassbyname() and the login_get* query
                    API (bool/enum/list/num/size/str/time/path/style).
- login_class.c     setusercontext(), setclasscontext(),
                    setlogincontext(), setclassenvironment(),
                    setclassresources(), setclasspriority().
- login_ok.c        auth_ttyok(), auth_hostok(), auth_timeok(),
                    auth_checknologin().
- login_times.c     parse_lt()/in_ltm()/in_ltms() time-range support.
- _secure_path.c    _secure_path(): root-owned/unwritable check used
                    when loading user .login_conf.
- login_cap.h       FreeBSD header vendored verbatim.

Darwin portability changes (all #ifdef __APPLE__ guarded):
- login_cap.c: add a static reallocarray() shim over realloc() with
  overflow checking; Darwin libc lacks it.
- getcap.c: rename libc-private _open/_read/_close to their public
  names; <db.h> from the macOS SDK supplies DB/dbopen for the .db
  fast path.
- login_class.c: neutralize facilities with no Darwin equivalent --
  sys/cpuset.h affinity handling (setclasscpumask/list2cpuset),
  sys/mac.h MAC labels (LOGIN_SETMAC), sys/rtprio.h realtime
  priorities (setpriority clamping fallback), setloginclass(2)
  (LOGIN_SETLOGINCLASS becomes a no-op), and FreeBSD-only rlimits
  (SBSIZE/VMEM/NPTS/SWAP/KQUEUES/UMTXP/PIPEBUF/VMM rows excluded).
- login_cap.h: include <sys/resource.h>/<stdint.h> so rlim_t resolves
  on Darwin.
- libutil.h: declare _secure_path() and the full cget* family; Darwin
  exposes no prototypes even though the SDK ships <db.h>.

Validation: all six sources compile warning-clean with clang -Wall
(one pre-existing upstream set-but-unused in login_ok.c left as-is);
the objects link into a working archive and an end-to-end probe
verified cgetent() record retrieval, continuation-line joining,
boolean and numeric capability lookup, and _secure_path().

Known follow-up: cgetent()'s cap_mkdb database path depends on the
SDK's deprecated Berkeley DB 1.85 <db.h>/dbopen().  If Apple removes
it, vendor FreeBSD's libc/db as its own module.  Text-mode
/etc/login.conf parsing does not use db at all.

Consumers need no Apple-extension shims: login(1)'s auth_pam() and
au_login_success/fail are self-contained inside the login tproj.
